#X obj 910 460 array set ockm-pat-\$1-on;
#X obj 910 700 tabwrite ockm-pat-\$1-on;
#X obj 1620 430 tabread ockm-pat-\$1-on;
#X obj 1620 460 tabwrite ockm-pat-\$1-on;
#X obj 1100 220 array get ockm-pat-\$1-acc;
#X obj 1100 260 array set ockm-bank-\$1-acc;
#X obj 1100 420 array get ockm-bank-\$1-acc 0 128;
#X obj 1100 460 array set ockm-pat-\$1-acc;
#X obj 1100 700 tabwrite ockm-pat-\$1-acc;
#X obj 1740 430 tabread ockm-pat-\$1-acc;
#X obj 1740 460 tabwrite ockm-pat-\$1-acc;
#X obj 1290 220 array get ockm-pat-\$1-slide;
#X obj 1290 260 array set ockm-bank-\$1-slide;
#X obj 1290 420 array get ockm-bank-\$1-slide 0 128;
#X obj 1290 460 array set ockm-pat-\$1-slide;
#X obj 1290 700 tabwrite ockm-pat-\$1-slide;
#X obj 1860 430 tabread ockm-pat-\$1-slide;
#X obj 1860 460 tabwrite ockm-pat-\$1-slide;
#X text 140 400 only lets the note through if the step is on;
#X text 420 100 glide into this note if the previous step had slide on;
#X text 720 530 edit one step: ockm-<track>-edit <step> <note> <on> <accent> <slide>;
#X text 1500 90 extend: repeat steps to fill a longer pattern;
